 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 3241,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Copies the 8-byte shape of digit $0A00+X from $58C2 to the pointer $85/$86 and moves the pointer on 8 bytes."
  },
  {
   "address": 4279,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Per-frame object update, skipped while the game is paused ($6443). Goes through the 11 slots: a slot in state 7 is only queued in the list at $1206; for the others, while the raster is above line $B4, it runs the player-attack test $10B2 and then the behaviour for the slot's state, through the table at $128B and a call whose operand is rewritten at $125F/$1260. The queued state 7 slots are then handled by $1D3E."
  },
  {
   "address": 8276,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Pause: when the key code in $8F44 is $50, sets $6443, waits for the key to be released, pressed again and released, then clears $6443."
  },
  {
   "address": 8486,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Mixes CIA 1's timer A, both bytes, with the previous result in $65CD and rotates it: a random number in A and $65CD. The low three bits of $DC04 are written into the offset of the branch at $65BE (at $65BF), which sets how many of the rotates at $65C0 are run."
  },
  {
   "address": 8935,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Reads the keyboard with CIA 1 into A. Returns $FF at once when any of the low five bits of $DC00 AND $DC01 reads low (the test at $8F4D, so while the joystick or a key in that range is down); otherwise scans the eight rows from $8F5B, looks the key up in the table at $8FBF and returns its code. $2127 keeps the result in $8F44."
  },
  {
   "address": 9959,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "[carry] Sets the eight sprite pointers in both screens' tables ($CFF8-$CFFF and $CBF8-$CBFF) to X, X+1, up to X+7."
  },
  {
   "address": 63424,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "The status panel's bitmap, which the raster interrupt irq_bottom switches on from line $CD (bitmap mode at $E000, multicolour): 40 cells wide, rows 19 to 24, 8 bytes a cell and 320 a row. [carry] Same bytes as level 2's panel_bitmap."
  },
  {
   "address": 63960,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Row 20, columns 27 to 31 (40 bytes): draw_timer ($755D) draws the three timer digits into the cells at $F9D8, $F9E8 and $F9F0. [carry] Same bytes as level 2's timer_cells."
  },
  {
   "address": 64048,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Row 20, columns 38 and 39, and row 21, columns 0 to 2: panel bitmap that no traced routine writes (40 bytes). [carry] Same bytes as level 2's panel_bitmap_2."
  },
  {
   "address": 64264,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Row 21, columns 25 to 31: panel bitmap that no traced routine writes (56 bytes). [carry] Same bytes as level 2's panel_bitmap_4."
  },
  {
   "address": 64688,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Row 22, columns 38 and 39, and row 23, columns 0 to 31: panel bitmap that no traced routine writes (272 bytes). [carry] Same bytes as level 2's panel_bitmap_6."
  },
  {
   "address": 64960,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "Row 23, columns 32 to 37: the fifth row of the panel picture (see panel_picture_0). [carry] Same bytes as level 2's panel_picture_4."
  }
 ]
